00:33:03.660 --> 00:33:05.660
That's not my fate.

00:33:05.660 --> 00:33:08.660
You cannot be a beacon of hope

00:33:08.660 --> 00:33:11.660
when you have darkness in your heart.

00:33:11.660 --> 00:33:13.660
And why did you send me back?

00:33:13.660 --> 00:33:15.660
Why did you give me a second chance?

00:33:15.660 --> 00:33:17.660
I didn't.

00:33:17.660 --> 00:33:21.660
It was not my decision to give you back your life.

00:33:21.660 --> 00:33:28.259
You may not see me as a hero.

00:33:28.259 --> 00:33:31.259
But the rest of the world does.

00:33:31.259 --> 00:33:33.539
And I did

00:33:33.539 --> 00:33:34.539
Die my feet.

00:33:34.539 --> 00:33:37.539
I regret as a father.

00:33:37.539 --> 00:33:40.539
My faith in you blinded me to the truth.

00:33:40.539 --> 00:33:43.539
You will never be earth's savior.

00:33:43.539 --> 00:34:18.289
Oh, it's your lucky day, Shamrock.

00:34:18.289 --> 00:34:19.289
I'm letting you go.

00:34:19.289 --> 00:34:23.019
Just like that, huh?

00:34:23.019 --> 00:34:27.510
See, I know, I'm disappointed.

00:34:27.510 --> 00:34:29.510
I was kind of holding out for a goodbye kiss from me.

00:34:29.510 --> 00:34:33.710
We're not done.

00:34:33.710 --> 00:34:37.500
I will hunt you and I will find you.

00:34:37.500 --> 00:34:39.500
You understand?

00:34:39.500 --> 00:34:42.500
You don't even know who I am.

00:34:42.500 --> 00:34:43.500
But I know who you are.

00:34:43.500 --> 00:34:45.500
You are.

00:34:45.500 --> 00:34:49.500
And I will be watching Green Arrow.

00:34:49.500 --> 00:35:25.269
Have you heard?

00:35:25.269 --> 00:35:28.269
Try to understand.

00:35:28.269 --> 00:35:31.269
It's all right.

00:35:31.269 --> 00:35:37.440
It gets easier

00:35:37.440 --> 00:35:41.260
I have changed

00:35:41.260 --> 00:35:47.780
and I've realized

00:35:47.780 --> 00:35:52.420
I was wrong

00:35:52.420 --> 00:35:53.420
now

00:35:56.420 --> 00:36:04.969
Oh, my love, I'd give anything.

00:36:04.969 --> 00:37:32.570
Ch chores, Clark.

00:37:32.570 --> 00:37:34.570
Work keeps a man honest.

00:37:34.570 --> 00:37:38.940
Gotta protect the things you worked hard to build.

00:37:38.940 --> 00:37:47.449
Are you real? I missed you.

00:37:47.449 --> 00:37:54.639
I never stopped watching out for you, Clark.

00:37:54.639 --> 00:37:55.639
Then you must be disappointed.

00:37:55.639 --> 00:38:01.099
I haven't grown into the man you raised me to be.

00:38:01.099 --> 00:38:03.099
No, you haven't.

00:38:03.099 --> 00:38:08.090
You are so much more than that.

00:38:08.090 --> 00:38:14.059
And I'm so proud of you, Clark.

00:38:14.059 --> 00:38:15.059
That's one, Dad.

00:38:15.059 --> 00:38:18.059
Since when do you start listening to Jarrell?

00:38:18.059 --> 00:38:21.360
Hmm?

00:38:21.360 --> 00:38:24.730
He's right.

00:38:24.730 --> 00:38:27.869
Give me a hand.

00:38:27.869 --> 00:38:32.750
I took my anger out on people.

00:38:32.750 --> 00:38:34.750
I destroyed an entire building.

00:38:34.750 --> 00:38:39.130
I know now that I have it within me to kill.

00:38:39.130 --> 00:38:41.130
I failed.

00:38:41.130 --> 00:38:44.130
We're all confronted with trials, son.

00:38:44.130 --> 00:38:47.130
But the true measure of a man

00:38:47.130 --> 00:38:50.130
is how he chooses to react in the face of those trials.

00:38:50.130 --> 00:38:51.130
You never had that problem.

00:38:51.130 --> 00:38:55.130
Come on, son, I'm so far away from perfect.

00:38:55.130 --> 00:38:58.130
I can never keep my own anger in check.

00:38:58.130 --> 00:39:02.130
I let it all build up inside me till it made my own heart give out.

00:39:02.130 --> 00:39:07.130
It was my fury, Clark, that drove me to want to kill another man.

00:39:07.130 --> 00:39:09.130
But instead, it killed me.

00:39:09.130 --> 00:39:14.659
Myel. Dad, you were just trying to protect me.

00:39:14.659 --> 00:39:17.659
We can't make excuses for the dark stains on our heart, son.

00:39:17.659 --> 00:39:20.659
I don't even know how I got to this place.

00:39:20.659 --> 00:39:22.659
We all make sacrifices, son.

00:39:22.659 --> 00:39:28.289
And every time we do, we lose a little something in the process.

00:39:28.289 --> 00:39:29.289
You've sacrificed.

00:39:29.289 --> 00:39:31.289
more than anybody.

00:39:31.289 --> 00:39:33.289
It'd be easy to let resentment build up inside,

00:39:33.289 --> 00:39:35.289
but it's got to come out somewhere.

00:39:35.289 --> 00:39:37.289
I feel like every time I do something right,

00:39:37.289 --> 00:39:38.289
I do something wrong.

00:39:38.289 --> 00:39:47.820
Sometimes I think it would be easier if you were here.

00:39:47.820 --> 00:39:52.730
Not a day goes by, Clark, when I don't regret

00:39:52.730 --> 00:39:55.730
not being able to be right here for you.

00:39:55.730 --> 00:39:58.360
I would do anything.

00:39:58.360 --> 00:40:00.360
I would give anything to be able to get a second chance

00:40:00.360 --> 00:40:03.699
to get it right.

00:40:03.699 --> 00:40:06.980
You got that second chance, son.

00:40:06.980 --> 00:40:09.980
You could be the greatest hero the world has ever known.

00:40:09.980 --> 00:40:14.670
Not according to Trell.

00:40:14.670 --> 00:40:15.670
Well, then do what you do.

00:40:15.670 --> 00:40:30.789
best prove him wrong.

00:40:30.789 --> 00:40:32.789
Jerell was right about one thing.

00:40:32.789 --> 00:40:35.789
Something dark is coming.

00:40:35.789 --> 00:40:37.789
You're going to be tested.

00:40:37.789 --> 00:40:43.610
It's not going to be easy, son.

00:40:43.610 --> 00:40:53.739
But I have faith in you.

00:40:53.739 --> 00:40:54.739
What's coming, Dad?

